{"name":"Angel’s Whisper","hex":"#dbdfd4","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"angel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An incorporeal and holy or semidivine messenger from a deity or other divine entity, traditionally depicted as a youthful, winged figure in flowing robes.\n\n One of the lowest order of such beings, below virtues.","One of the lowest order of such beings, below virtues."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To support by donating money."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angel"},{"term":"whisper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of speaking in a quiet voice, especially without vibration of the vocal cords; the sound thus produced.","A rumor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To speak softly or under one's breath, so as to be heard only by one near at hand; to utter words without sonant breath; to talk without that vibration of the vocal cords which gives sonorous, or vocal, sound.","To say (something) softly or under one's breath, so as to be heard only by one near at hand; to utter (something) without sonant breath, without that vibration of the vocal cords which gives sonorous, or vocal, sound."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whisper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Whispering","blocks":[{"text":"Whispering is an unvoiced mode of phonation in which the vocal cords are abducted so that they do not vibrate; air passes between the arytenoid cartilages to create audible turbulence during speech. Supralaryngeal articulation remains the same as in normal speech."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whispering"},{"title":"Angel","blocks":[{"text":"An angel is a spiritual, heavenly, or supernatural entity, often depicted as humanoid with bird-like wings, frequently in the role as a messenger or intermediary between God and humanity in various traditions like the Abrahamic religions. Other roles include protectors and guides for humans, such as guardian angels, and servants of 